hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3028","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Yahya, narrated to us Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: My father narrated to me, that Aishah (RA) informed me, who said:

""We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the time of the new moon of Dhu al-Hijjah. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever wishes to enter ihram for 'Umrah may do so, and whoever wishes to enter ihram for Hajj may do so.' If I had not brought a sacrificial animal, I would have entered ihram for 'Umrah.'

So some of us entered ihram for 'Umrah and others for Hajj. Then I menstruated before entering Makkah. I was still menstruating on the Day of 'Arafah, so I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said: 'Leave your 'Umrah, undo your hair, comb it, and enter ihram for Hajj.'

When the night of al-Hasbah came, he sent 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr with me to al-Tan'im. He mounted me behind him, and I entered ihram for 'Umrah in place of my previous 'Umrah. Thus, Allah decreed that my Hajj and 'Umrah were complete. There was no sacrificial animal, fasting, or charity required in any of that.""

Abu Bakr (RA) said: ""I have clarified in the matter which I dictated in the compilation regarding the reconciliation between the reports about the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ) that Aishah (RA) only left the actions for her 'Umrah because she was unable to perform the tawaf around the House due to her menstruation, not that she abandoned that 'Umrah. I have clarified in that context that the Prophet's (ﷺ) statement to her, 'Your tawaf is sufficient for your Hajj and 'Umrah,' indicates that she did not abandon her 'Umrah. Rather, she only left the actions for it because she was menstruating and unable to perform the tawaf.

I have also clarified that his statement, 'There was no sacrificial animal, charity, or fasting required in any of that,' means that there was no sacrificial animal, charity, or fasting required for the 'Umrah that I performed after the Hajj. The evidence for the correctness of this interpretation is that the Prophet (ﷺ) had already slaughtered a cow on behalf of his wives before Aishah (RA) performed this 'Umrah from al-Tan'im. Did you not hear her say: 'When the Day of Sacrifice came, meat of a cow was brought to us. We asked, ""What is this?"" and it was said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) has slaughtered a cow on behalf of his wives.""'

Thus, Aishah (RA) informed that there had been a sacrificial animal in her Hajj before she performed the 'Umrah from al-Tan'im.""

In the report of Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah (RA), she said at the end of the report: ""Meaning the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Go out with 'Abd al-Rahman to al-Tan'im and enter ihram for your 'Umrah.' So I did, and then I did not offer any sacrificial animal."""
"3029","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Tamam, narrated to us Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bukayr, Maymun ibn Makhramah narrated to me on the authority of his father, who said: I also heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal saying, I heard Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrating on the authority of 'Urwah, who said: I heard 'A'ishah (RA) and he mentioned a long story, and he mentioned these words which I have mentioned at the end of the report. He said: And he said, I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrating on the authority of 'Urwah, on the authority of 'A'ishah (RA), that she informed them about their 'umrah after the Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She said: ""I menstruated and then performed 'umrah after the Hajj. Then I did not fast, nor did I offer a sacrificial animal.""

Abu Bakr (a narrator) said: This report clarifies that she intended that she did not fast nor offer a sacrificial animal after that 'umrah which she performed from al-Tan'im, not before it.

**CHAPTER:**"
